neration Nintendo games to the GBA the  very games that had their first comeback  in WarioWare just one year later we  would get WarioWare twisted the crazy  innovation this time was a cartridge  with a built-in gyro sensor which meant  you had to complete many of the games  using simple motion controls this was  two full years before the we brought  motion controls to the living room  twisted was certainly inspired by kirby  tilt and tumble and that did predate  warioware by a few years but Wario did  punt the little pink puffball out of the  way when we came around with an  innovative launch game as Nintendo has  want to do with its first party games  Wario Ware smooth moves demonstrated the  full potential of the technology with  over twenty different uses of the Wii  mote across its minigames there was the  typical sword slashing and pointing  Shore but smooth moves mix things up  with more creative poses like holding  the remote above your head rotating in  your palm like a joystick or even  completely discarding it only to quickly  draw at a moment later that quick draw  would be featured again when a certain  switch launch game came around one to  switch features many of those same  motion configurations and takes things  to the next level with new technology  like the joy Kahn's HD Rumble but the  WarioWare influence is clear in the  gameplay humor and even the art style  whether it was motion control at home or  on the go Wario Ware showed Nintendo  fans the possibilities  that wasn't Wario's only launch game  either WarioWare touched came alongside  the DS  and as you'd expect it once again showed  off what in tendo's tech could do  minigames capitalized on the touchscreen  with taps drags rubs and all other  manner of stylus control touchscreen  gaming continued to be a Nintendo staple  through the three DS Wii U and now  switch but the DS did at first and  WarioWare proved it could work Wario's  final outing on the DS continued to  innovate WarioWare DIY